  "body": "Expose trunnion kinematics fields in the Machine Editor, capture the setup WCS-to-trunnion-pivot offset, and ship a verified XYZAC Mach4 example machine file.\n\n### Context\n- `crates/app/src/machine/fields.rs` and `sheet.rs` do not show rotary `pivot`, child `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, or `controller.rtcp`.\n- `assets/machines/` contains no 5-axis AC trunnion sample file today.\n- Because non-RTCP table-table kinematics depend on where the setup `G54` origin sits relative to the `C` platter and `A` pivot (`crates/app/src/rotary_stack.rs` precedent for `SetupDef::nose_to_axis`), a setup needs an explicit datum-to-pivot offset instead of silently assuming `[0, 0, 0]`.\n- Depends on schema (#1962), AC IK solver (#1965), and `mach4.cps` (#1968 or sibling post issue).\n\n### Requirements\n- Add editable fields and read-only rows for rotary `pivot`, `offset`, `zero_offset`, `rollover`, and `controller.rtcp` in `fields.rs` and `sheet.rs`.\n- Add a setup datum-to-pivot offset field (and calibrated-at-pivot option) used by the IK solver and refused by name when omitted on a non-RTCP multi-axis job.\n- Add a clean-room XYZAC Mach4 trunnion sample machine under `assets/machines/` and register it in `crates/app/src/posting.rs`.\n\nDone means: Users can edit and validate AC trunnion parameters in the Machine pane, state setup WCS-to-pivot offsets without silent zeros, and pass `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` with the new XYZAC sample.\n\nPart of #1958\n",
